&lt;h3&gt;


  The mathematical pipeline
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;pre data-lang="mermaid"&gt;&lt;code&gt;flowchart LR
    A[Technique ID + seed + difficulty] --&amp;gt; B[Generator]
    B --&amp;gt; C[Question + expected answer]
    C --&amp;gt; D[Independent solver]
    D --&amp;gt; E{Answers match?}
    E --&amp;gt;|No| F[CROSS_VALIDATION_FAILED]
    E --&amp;gt;|Yes| G[Structured explanation]
    G --&amp;gt; H[Stored server question]
    H --&amp;gt; I[User answer]
    I --&amp;gt; J[Safe normalization]
    J --&amp;gt; K[Verified attempt]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


  Difficulty and mastery
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Adaptive learning is deterministic rather than artificial intelligence. It uses persisted facts:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;recent correctness;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;recent accuracy;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;response time;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;consecutive mistakes;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;mastery score;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;review date;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;prerequisite gaps;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;technique history.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The result is explainable. A recommendation can say:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Practice this technique because your recent accuracy is low or your review date is overdue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It does not claim that a hidden AI model made the decision.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The bugs and design decisions that mattered
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  A client must not be able to award itself XP
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The original UI contains local gameplay state for compatibility with the approved frontend. The production learning API does not trust that state. The backend ignores client-provided learning outcomes in the compatibility sync route and calculates outcomes from verified events.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  A generated question must fail loudly when mathematics disagrees
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The math engine does not silently accept a mismatched solver or explanation. A generator/solver mismatch throws &lt;code&gt;CROSS_VALIDATION_FAILED&lt;/code&gt;, which makes the error visible in tests and logs instead of teaching an incorrect answer.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  A duplicate request must not duplicate a reward
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Attempt uniqueness, session completion claiming, and XP transaction idempotency are separate protections. This matters because users retry network requests, mobile browsers reconnect, and two tabs can submit the same completion.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Responsive behavior is part of correctness
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The frontend was kept visually consistent while fixing practical issues:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;desktop sidebar width and content offset now use the same valid spacing;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;mobile drawer width adapts to narrow viewports;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;bottom navigation respects safe-area insets;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;page shells prevent accidental horizontal overflow;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;navigation labels truncate safely on very small screens;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;reduced-motion preferences are respected;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;invalid fractional icon utilities were replaced with reliable sizes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Why Does Open Innovation Matter?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;VedaX does not use a hosted AI model and does not pretend to. Its open-source value is in making the educational and mathematical boundaries inspectable:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributors can audit the exact generator, solver, explanation, and verification code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;New techniques can be added through a documented process instead of a hidden content pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributors can add randomized mathematics tests and reproduce failures with deterministic seeds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The server-authoritative learning rules are visible and reviewable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The frontend can be improved without replacing the backend learning contract.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The project deliberately uses deterministic learning heuristics rather than calling them AI. That keeps recommendations reproducible and makes a wrong result easier to diagnose.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  AI Disclosure
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;VedaX does not currently use a generative AI model, remote AI API, or AI-generated answer path in its runtime. Mathematical generation, answer checking, mastery, recommendations, and adaptive difficulty are deterministic application code.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If a future contributor adds an AI-assisted educational feature, it must remain separate from authoritative correctness and reward calculations, be documented in this section, and include tests for unavailable or incorrect model responses.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  My Agent Session
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This project was developed through repository-driven implementation and verification. The important reproducibility boundary is the checked-in code and test suite, not an unverified assistant transcript.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The repository records the implementation through:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;focused conventional commits;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;pinned Node.js and lockfiles;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;offline backend tests;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;frontend typecheck, lint, and build commands;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CI configuration;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;architecture, security, release, and contributor documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;No public agent-session transcript is linked because none is required to rebuild or review the application.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  My First User
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This repository does not claim a verified paying customer or testimonial. The intended first users are:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;students learning mental arithmetic;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;teachers who want structured supplementary practice;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;competitive-exam learners;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;educators contributing new examples or technique tests;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;open-source contributors interested in trustworthy educational software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The first useful milestone is not a fabricated growth number. It is a learner completing a technique, understanding the explanation, and returning to practice the next review item.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Prize Categories / Challenge Fit
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The following are the honest project categories VedaX fits. They should be adjusted to the exact event requirements before publishing a challenge submission:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Education
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;VedaX turns a traditional mathematical system into an interactive, measurable learning workflow.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Open Source
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The repository includes contributor documentation, a technique guide, issue forms, a pull request template, CI, and reproducible setup instructions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Testing and Trustworthy Software
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The project treats mathematical cross-validation, server authority, idempotency, and security tests as core product functionality rather than optional cleanup.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Responsive Web Application
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The approved VedaX interface works across desktop, tablet, and mobile layouts without replacing the existing design direction.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Who Would Use This?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;VedaX is useful for people who want a repeatable way to practice rather than a one-time calculator:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Students:&lt;/strong&gt; learn one sutra, see an example, and practice it immediately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Teachers:&lt;/strong&gt; use the technique catalog and mastery data as supplementary practice material.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Exam learners:&lt;/strong&gt; build speed and accuracy through timed sessions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Math enthusiasts:&lt;/strong&gt; compare different mental calculation strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Contributors:&lt;/strong&gt; add a mathematically validated technique or improve the test suite.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The project is not a replacement for a teacher, curriculum, or conventional mathematics education. It is a practice and explanation tool.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Team Submissions
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;VedaX is maintained as a single repository. If this project is submitted as a team entry, add the participating DEV/GitHub usernames here before publishing the submission. No team member names are invented in this README.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Verification and deployment
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Backend tests
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;make &lt;span class="nb"&gt;test&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The backend suite covers authentication, protected routes, profile field protection, leaderboard authority, malformed requests, learning utilities, scoring, streaks, stable technique IDs, deterministic generation, randomized cross-validation, normalization, and explanation structure.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Frontend checks
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;make frontend-typecheck
make frontend-lint
make frontend-build
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


  Dependency audit
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;npm &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--prefix&lt;/span&gt; backend audit &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--omit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;dev
npm &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--prefix&lt;/span&gt; frontend audit &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--omit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;dev
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The backend production audit is clean. The frontend has two deferred moderate React Router advisories whose available fix requires a breaking upgrade. That upgrade is intentionally separate from the approved frontend/responsive maintenance work.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Docker
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;docker build &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-t&lt;/span&gt; vedax &lt;span class="nb"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;
docker run &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--rm&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-p&lt;/span&gt; 5000:5000 &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--env-file&lt;/span&gt; backend/.env vedax
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The Dockerfile builds the frontend artifact and runs the backend. Docker verification must be performed in an environment with Docker installed and a transaction-capable MongoDB deployment.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Installation
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Requirements
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Node.js &lt;code&gt;22.23.3&lt;/code&gt; from &lt;code&gt;.nvmrc&lt;/code&gt;;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;npm;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MongoDB for local backend runtime;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Docker only if using the container workflow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Install dependencies
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;npm ci
npm &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--prefix&lt;/span&gt; frontend ci
npm &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--prefix&lt;/span&gt; backend ci
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


  Configure environment files
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;cp &lt;/span&gt;backend/.env.example backend/.env
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;cp &lt;/span&gt;frontend/.env.example frontend/.env.local
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Set a local MongoDB connection string and a development JWT secret in &lt;code&gt;backend/.env&lt;/code&gt;. Never commit the resulting &lt;code&gt;.env&lt;/code&gt; files.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Environment variables
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Backend
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
